WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.062
Business continuity in operational technology is the ability to maintain or restore

00:00:05.062 --> 00:00:08.783
critical physical operations at an acceptable level after disruption.

00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:13.332
The mission may be safe production, electricity delivery, water treatment, transportation,

00:00:13.332 --> 00:00:17.467
environmental control, or another service that depends on people, equipment,

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.534
and control systems working together.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:23.669
Continuity does not always mean keeping every system fully available.

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:29.458
A site may shift to a safe degraded mode, reduce capacity, isolate a process,

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:32.766
use alternate equipment, or perform a controlled shutdown.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:38.142
Plans define the minimum acceptable operation and the conditions for returning to normal.

00:00:38.142 --> 00:00:43.104
IT service continuity often focuses on restoring applications, data, and user access.

00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:48.066
OT continuity includes those concerns but also considers process state, equipment sequencing,

00:00:48.066 --> 00:00:51.374
utility dependencies, operator visibility, product quality, environmental consequence,

00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:54.268
and the safety of shutdown and restart.

00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:59.644
Disaster recovery and incident response support continuity but are not identical to it.

00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:01.711
Recovery restores technology and data.

00:01:01.711 --> 00:01:04.606
Incident response contains and investigates an event.

00:01:04.606 --> 00:01:10.395
Continuity coordinates the broader operational choices that protect the mission while those activities occur.

00:01:10.395 --> 00:01:12.462
Safety comes before production pressure.

00:01:12.462 --> 00:01:17.838
A fast technical recovery is not successful if process conditions, logic integrity, alarms,

00:01:17.838 --> 00:01:21.146
interlocks, or field equipment have not been validated.

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:25.694
Operations and engineering need authority to decide when restoration is safe.

00:01:25.694 --> 00:01:30.656
A useful continuity plan connects critical processes to assets, people, vendors, spares,

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:34.378
utilities, communications, backups, fallback procedures, and tested recovery sequences.

00:01:34.378 --> 00:01:40.580
It prepares the organization to make deliberate decisions when normal automation and information are unavailable.
